# Secret group `side-role`: The `alldots_side` role password and connection string.
# Loaded by: alldots-ai-gateway.service, alldots-restore-test.service.
#
# Ownership and mode are load-bearing: `root:root 0600`. systemd reads EnvironmentFile= as root
# before dropping privileges. provision.sh installs this template to
# /opt/alldots/shared/env/side-role.env only when that file does not exist, so an operator's values are
# never overwritten by a rerun, and it never prints a value. A key belongs to exactly one group
# (docs/architecture/delivery-and-operations.md); this file is excluded from restic backups.

# ALLDOTS_SIDE_DB_PASSWORD: the password the operator sets with
# `ALTER ROLE alldots_side WITH PASSWORD '...'` (migration 0040_least_privilege_roles.sql creates
# the role itself, with no password until this is done). Distinct from ALLDOTS_DATA_DB_PASSWORD in
# data-role.env, so the two roles are never accidentally given the same password. Used, together
# with POSTGRES_DB in postgres.env, to build the connection string below.
ALLDOTS_SIDE_DB_PASSWORD=

# ALLDOTS_SIDE_DATABASE_URL: shared by every `alldots_side`-role process (alldots-ai-gateway and
# the restore test, per docs/operations/database-roles.md) — none of them ever writes a
# choke-point table, so one read-only-on-choke-point, full-on-side-tables role covers all of
# them. Built from
# ALLDOTS_SIDE_DB_PASSWORD above, e.g.:
# postgres://alldots_side:<ALLDOTS_SIDE_DB_PASSWORD>@127.0.0.1:5432/alldots
ALLDOTS_SIDE_DATABASE_URL=
